Align local devcontainer user IDs

Honor updateRemoteUserUID as a tri-state setting. On Linux localhost
engines, default to aligning the effective container user when the agent
service has a bind mount, allow true to force alignment, and allow false
to disable it. Warn and leave image IDs unchanged on unsupported hosts.

Perform account and home ownership migration in the prepared-image layer
without requiring user-management tools from the base image. Detect UID
collisions, preserve the image GID when the requested GID is occupied,
and include the selected IDs in prepared-image cache keys.

Cover the policy, Compose mounts, ownership migration, collisions, and
unsupported hosts with integration tests.
